-> Test: native module emission — FireException handler emits an Exception particle.
link native_modules/libtest_helper.so as helper

-> Define local handler for emitted Exception particles. No local schema
-> declaration needed — handler dispatch is purely _class-based (T30).
-> The native module's own "Exception" type (source/message — deliberately
-> not the language's built-in Exception, a different shape) is already
-> registered at the qualified `helper.Exception`, used below for the
-> return.
Exception => {
    assert source = "test_helper"
    assert message = "something went wrong"
    return helper.Exception { source = source, message = message }
}

-> Invoking FireException handler emits an Exception particle.
req = helper.FireException { message = "something went wrong" }
emit req to helper get _
